  "result": "Excellent! All 157 tests pass. I've successfully added payment terms support to invoices with automatic due date calculation.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **Added TERMS_INVALID error** to src/errors.js for invalid payment terms\n\n2. **Updated createInvoice()** to:\n   - Accept optional `terms` parameter: 'NET14', 'NET30' (default), or 'EOM'\n   - Calculate due date based on terms\n   - Store both `terms` and `dueDate` on the invoice\n   - Return TERMS_INVALID error for unknown terms\n\n3. **Implemented due date calculation**:\n   - **NET14**: issue date + 14 days\n   - **NET30**: issue date + 30 days (default)\n   - **EOM**: last day of the invoice month\n   - Correctly handles month/year boundaries and leap years\n\n4. **Added 12 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Default NET30 terms\n   - NET14, NET30, and EOM term types\n   - EOM on various days (1st, last, 31-day, 30-day months)\n   - Month and year boundary crossings\n   - Leap year handling\n   - Invalid terms rejection\n\nThe implementation:\n- Never mutates input invoices\n- Uses existing date utilities for consistency\n- Handles all edge cases (leap years, month boundaries)\n- Works seamlessly with existing invoice features (discounts, VAT, tier pricing)",
